---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "The Palmetto Cafe",
  servesCuisine: ["Contemporary American", "Southern Lowcountry"],
  priceRange: "$$$",
  telephone: "+1-843-724-8131",
  url: "https://charlestonplace.com/food-beverage/the-palmetto-cafe/",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "205 Meeting Street",
    addressLocality: "Charleston",
    addressRegion: "SC",
    postalCode: "29401",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "The Palmetto Cafe at The Charleston Place — a sunlit Lowcountry dining room serving breakfast, lunch, and Sunday brunch, known for shrimp & grits, she crab soup, and the Palmetto sampler. No official itemized price menu is published.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Palmetto Cafe Menu Guide (2026) — The Charleston Place, Charleston | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to The Palmetto Cafe at The Charleston Place, Charleston: hours, signature Lowcountry dishes, and the honest story on prices (no official itemized menu prices published)."
  path="/palmetto-cafe-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/palmetto-cafe-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/palmetto-cafe-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a sunlit Southern Lowcountry veranda restaurant with ceiling fans, wicker chairs and white tablecloths at breakfast (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Charleston, SC
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      The Palmetto Cafe — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The Palmetto Cafe is the all-day dining room of <strong>The Charleston Place</strong>
      at 205 Meeting Street — the hotel's sunny, veranda-style answer to Lowcountry
      cooking, serving breakfast, lunch, and Sunday brunch. It steps into the spotlight
      this year: the hotel's flagship restaurant, The Charleston Grill, served its final
      dinner in August 2025 after 36 years, and the Palmetto Cafe now carries the
      torch as the property's main restaurant (a new Charleston Grill replacement
      concept is planned but not yet open). The honest headline first: <strong>the
      restaurant publishes no itemized online price menu</strong> — official pages list
      dishes and hours, not prices — so this guide covers the menu shape, hours, and
      era-dated reported figures. Everything is written in our own words.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">205 Meeting St, Charleston, SC 29401 (The Charleston Place)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive chef Steven Manall (per OpenTable profile; not on the official site)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Contemporary American / Southern Lowcountry</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">$$$ — OpenTable band $31–$50 per person; no official itemized prices published</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">No confirmed online booking link; reserve by phone — 843-724-8131 (restaurant) or 1-800-611-5545</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Recognition</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">AAA Four Diamond per the Charleston Area CVB (not claimed on the restaurant's own site); OpenTable "Top 100 Brunch Restaurants in America" list (2023 era)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Per the official Charleston Place page, fetched 2026-10-01:
        <strong>breakfast daily 7:00–11:00 AM; lunch daily 12:00–3:00 PM; Sunday
        à la carte brunch 10:00 AM–3:00 PM.</strong> Note that third-party listings
        (including OpenTable) show slightly different hours — treat those as stale
        and go with the hotel's own page.
      </p>

      <h2>Signature dishes</h2>
      <p>
        The dishes reviewers and third-party menus keep coming back to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Lowcountry Shrimp and Grits</strong>: the house's signature Southern plate.</li>
        <li><strong>She Crab Soup</strong>: the classic Lowcountry soup, finished with sherry.</li>
        <li><strong>Seafood Club</strong>: lobster, shrimp, applewood-smoked bacon, smoked salmon, and tomato.</li>
        <li><strong>Palmetto Sampler</strong>: a tasting plate of crab cake, she crab soup, chicken salad, '21' burger, and fries.</li>
        <li><strong>Crab Cake Benedict</strong>: a reviewer favorite at breakfast.</li>
        <li><strong>'21' Burger</strong>: inspired by the '21' Club, the hotel's former sister property.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Third-party 2026-era menus also list eggs Benedict ($18), steak and eggs
        ($22), a Palmetto omelet with crab and lobster ($19), and a jumbo lump
        crab cake ($16) — all figures below are reported, not official.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Breakfast:</strong> the crab cake Benedict — it's the dish reviewers name most.</li>
        <li><strong>Lunch:</strong> the shrimp &amp; grits for the Lowcountry experience, or the seafood club.</li>
        <li><strong>The sampler play:</strong> the Palmetto sampler ($29 reported) covers four signatures in one plate.</li>
        <li><strong>Soup first:</strong> start with the she crab soup ($12 reported) with its sherry pour.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Call ahead:</strong> with no confirmed online booking, phone is the reliable path — 843-724-8131.</li>
        <li><strong>No public price list:</strong> the restaurant publishes no itemized prices, so ask about current pricing when you book if budget matters.</li>
        <li><strong>Sunday brunch</strong> (10 AM–3 PM) is the week's signature service — and landed the restaurant on OpenTable's national Top 100 brunch list.</li>
        <li><strong>Same-hotel note:</strong> the Charleston Grill closed in August 2025; don't follow outdated guides to a restaurant that no longer exists.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://charlestonplace.com/food-beverage/the-palmetto-cafe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — The Palmetto Cafe</a> (hours; phone reservations 843-724-8131)</li>
        <li><a href="https://charlestonplace.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official hotel page — The Charleston Place</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://charlestonplace.com/dining/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">All Charleston Place dining</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        The Palmetto Cafe publishes <strong>no itemized online price menu</strong> —
        said plainly, not guessed. The figures referenced here (shrimp &amp; grits
        $18, she crab soup $12, seafood club $29, Palmetto sampler $29) are
        third-party reported prices from 2026-era menu aggregators, corroborated by
        2023-era figures suggesting stable pricing — but they are not the
        restaurant's own numbers. Always verify with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More South Carolina guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-south-carolina/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in South Carolina →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/peninsula-grill-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Peninsula Grill</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Lowcountry fine dining at Planters Inn (temporarily closed for renovation)</span></li>
        <li><a href="/circa-1886-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Circa 1886</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— tasting-menu fine dining at Wentworth Mansion</span></li>
        <li><a href="/gabrielle-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Gabrielle</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— "Stylishly Southern" at Hotel Bennett</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
